1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,640
So with Pi installed and you logged in and

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:05,920
an AI model connected, the next important

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:08,400
step is to check the settings and make

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,400
sure that everything is configured the way

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,760
you want it to be configured.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,200
You can run slash settings to tweak some

7
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,800
of the most important settings here.

8
00:00:17,398 --> 00:00:20,198
You can, for example, enable or disable

9
00:00:20,278 --> 00:00:21,238
auto compaction.

10
00:00:21,398 --> 00:00:23,878
You can simply select the setting and hit

11
00:00:23,958 --> 00:00:27,078
Enter or Space to toggle the different

12
00:00:27,158 --> 00:00:27,878
options here.

13
00:00:28,343 --> 00:00:30,583
Auto compaction, for example, means that

14
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:32,983
if you exceed the context window of the

15
00:00:32,983 --> 00:00:36,103
model you get connected, the Pi Agent will

16
00:00:36,103 --> 00:00:39,143
automatically summarize the conversation

17
00:00:39,143 --> 00:00:40,263
you had thus far.

18
00:00:40,263 --> 00:00:42,743
That's a process called compaction, and it

19
00:00:42,743 --> 00:00:44,583
gets triggered automatically if that

20
00:00:44,583 --> 00:00:45,783
setting is set to true.

21
00:00:45,783 --> 00:00:47,143
And therefore, you want to typically have

22
00:00:47,143 --> 00:00:47,863
it set to true.

23
00:00:48,455 --> 00:00:50,935
Now you'll see there is a broad variety of

24
00:00:50,935 --> 00:00:52,935
options here, and those options also will

25
00:00:52,935 --> 00:00:53,895
change over time.

26
00:00:54,295 --> 00:00:57,175
The defaults will very likely be fine.

27
00:00:57,335 --> 00:00:59,495
It's nonetheless worth taking a look

28
00:00:59,575 --> 00:01:01,495
through them and tweaking them to your

29
00:01:01,495 --> 00:01:02,055
liking.

30
00:01:02,055 --> 00:01:04,455
For example, you could hide the thinking

31
00:01:04,455 --> 00:01:07,095
blocks if you don't want those to clutter

32
00:01:07,095 --> 00:01:09,255
up the output that's shown on the screen

33
00:01:09,255 --> 00:01:10,855
when the agent operates and does

34
00:01:10,935 --> 00:01:11,415
something.

35
00:01:12,281 --> 00:01:14,441
Also, interesting might be the telemetry

36
00:01:14,441 --> 00:01:17,881
one, where you can actually disable it to

37
00:01:18,041 --> 00:01:20,921
not send anonymous version and update

38
00:01:20,921 --> 00:01:21,721
information

39
00:01:22,227 --> 00:01:24,627
to the providers of Pi.

40
00:01:24,627 --> 00:01:25,427
Now, very important.

41
00:01:25,427 --> 00:01:27,827
This is not referring to your prompts or

42
00:01:27,827 --> 00:01:28,627
your data.

43
00:01:28,787 --> 00:01:30,947
That's just going to be sent to the model

44
00:01:30,947 --> 00:01:32,947
provider for the model to do its work.

45
00:01:33,347 --> 00:01:35,267
This is not being sent to the people

46
00:01:35,267 --> 00:01:37,987
behind Pi, but that is referring to that

47
00:01:37,987 --> 00:01:38,867
telemetry option.

48
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:40,947
You can still disable it if you don't want

49
00:01:40,947 --> 00:01:41,987
to send anything.

50
00:01:42,574 --> 00:01:44,334
Also interesting is the theme.

51
00:01:44,494 --> 00:01:47,054
There are two built-in themes at the point

52
00:01:47,054 --> 00:01:49,054
of time where I'm recording this: the dark

53
00:01:49,054 --> 00:01:51,934
theme, or if you switch it, the light

54
00:01:51,934 --> 00:01:52,974
theme, or automatic.

55
00:01:52,974 --> 00:01:54,974
If you want to base it on your system

56
00:01:54,974 --> 00:01:57,614
settings, you can change that here.

57
00:01:58,094 --> 00:01:59,534
Would have to restart for that to have

58
00:01:59,534 --> 00:01:59,934
effect.

59
00:02:00,014 --> 00:02:01,534
I'll stick to dark though.

60
00:02:02,334 --> 00:02:03,934
So these are some of the settings you can

61
00:02:03,934 --> 00:02:04,254
tweak.

62
00:02:04,494 --> 00:02:07,294
There is something else you can tweak, and

63
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:08,894
you should be aware of when it comes to

64
00:02:08,894 --> 00:02:10,014
configuring Pi.
